-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura map from H¹ onto the dual of J₀(M')[𝔪]
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, $k$ a field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\mathcal O\to k$ surjective, $p\neq 2$ a prime with $\operatorname{char}k=p$, and $M'\neq 0$ a natural number with $p\nmid M'$; let $S$ be a finite set of naturals. Write $H^1=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(M',\top),\mathcal O)$ for the additive homomorphisms from the abelianisation-free group $\Gamma_H(M',\top)\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ (the subgroup attached to $H=\top$, i.e. $\Gamma_0(M')$) to $\mathcal O$. The generators [`CohCarrier.Gen`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) are symbols $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid M'$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid M'$) and $\langle d\rangle$ ($d\in(\mathbb Z/M')^\times$), and `opFamily` sends them to the endomorphisms `heckeTL` at $\ell$ resp. $q$ and `diamondL` at $d$ of $H^1$; assume these operators commute pairwise (hypothesis `hcomm`), and let $\bar\theta$ assign to each generator an element of $k$. Let $\mathbb T$ be the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(H^1)$ generated by these operators, let $S'$ be an `IdempotentSplitting` of $\mathbb T$ (a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals and satisfying $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j\iff i\neq j$), fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0}\mathbb T e_{i_0}$ to $k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0})=\bar\theta(g)$ for every generator $g$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ factoring through a finite level) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant subspace other than $0$ and everything, and assume the trace condition: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$, $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)=\bar\theta(T_\ell)$. Then there are a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of `HeckeAlg` $=\mathbb Z[X_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathrm{HeckeAlg}/\mathfrak m\to k$ such that $p\in\mathfrak m$ and $\iota(X_\ell\bmod\mathfrak m)=\bar\theta(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$, and, with $k$ an algebra over $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}/\mathfrak m$ via $\iota$ and $J_0(M')=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$M'$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ carrying the `heckeModuleBar` action, there is an additive map $$\Psi:H^1\longrightarrow \mathrm{Hom}_k\bigl(k\otimes_{\mathrm{HeckeAlg}/\mathfrak m}J_0(M')[\mathfrak m],k\bigr)$$ (the $\mathfrak m$-torsion being `torsionBySet`) with: $\Psi(t\cdot v)=\pi_k(e_{i_0}te_{i_0})\,\Psi(v)$ for all $t\in\mathbb T$ and $v\in H^1$; $\Psi$ surjective; and for $m$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H^1$, $\Psi(m)=0$ if and only if $m$ lies in the $e_{i_0}\mathbb T e_{i_0}$-span of the elements $a\cdot n$ with $\pi_k(a)=0$ and $n\in e_{i_0}H^1$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura comparison in the form needed for multiplicity-one arguments: the group cohomology of $\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathcal O$-coefficients maps onto the $k$-dual of the $\mathfrak m$-torsion of the Jacobian $J_0(M')$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, equivariantly for the corner character $\pi_k$, with kernel on the corner exactly $(\ker\pi_k)\cdot e_{i_0}H^1$; the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of the abstract Hecke algebra is produced from the eigensystem $\bar\theta$ and the trace condition on $\bar\rho$. It is used by [`CohCarrier.exists_span_pair_union_ker_smul_eq_top_cornerSubmodule_H1_top_of_isAbsolutelyIrreducible`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_span_pair_union_ker_smul_eq_top_cornerSubmodule_H1_top_of_isAbsolutelyIrreducible) to bound the number of generators of the corner module.
